## 1. Setup

### 1.1 The substrate

The WIN Paradigm identifies the vacuum substrate with an 8×8 torus lattice (64 sites) with periodic boundary conditions.

### 1.2 The particle multiplet

The discrete 5-point Laplacian on the 8×8 torus has eigenvalue

$$\lambda(n_1, n_2) = 4 - 2\cos\left(\frac{2\pi n_1}{8}\right) - 2\cos\left(\frac{2\pi n_2}{8}\right)$$

At λ = 4, the equation reduces to

$$\cos\left(\frac{\pi n_1}{4}\right) + \cos\left(\frac{\pi n_2}{4}\right) = 0$$

which has **exactly 14 solutions** in (n₁, n₂) ∈ {0, …, 7}². These 14 modes are the particle multiplet.

### 1.3 The 14 modes

The 14 modes at λ = 4, with their (n₁, n₂) quantum numbers, are:

