The mode vectors on the 8×8 torus have three support values. That these equal the framework constants N, V, N/2 is derived. Whether there is a deeper reason — a symmetry or a conservation law — is open.

### 6.2 Why does n₁ order the shells?

The shells increase with n₁. This is a "processing direction" on the torus. The physical meaning is not yet derived.

### 6.3 Is the rule independent of the entropy-rank assignment?

The paper assigns modes to particles by entropy rank. The derived shell rule uses the observed particle masses to fix the assignment. Whether the entropy-rank ordering is the same as the mass ordering for all 14 particles is a separate check.

### 6.4 What does the support physically represent?

The support is the number of lattice sites with non-negligible amplitude. Physically, this could represent the mode's "footprint" on the substrate, or the number of substrate sites involved in processing the mode.

